        "original_id": "a56686ab-e9ce-50f0-a742-984ab8eda15c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mariana Kovacevic, Asamoah Gyan\n- Roles: traditional healer, professional footballer, striker, captain\n- Teams: Kayserispor, Ghana national team\n- Events: 2012 African Cup of Nations\n- Places: Gabon, Equatorial Guinea, Accra, Ghana, Serbia\n- Treatments: horse placenta treatment\n\nFacts:\n- Asamoah Gyan was born on 22 November 1985 in Accra.\n- Mariana Kovacevic is a Serbian traditional healer who specializes in using horse placenta treatment to heal athletes.\n- During the 2012 African Cup of Nations in Gabon and Equatorial Guinea, Mariana Kovacevic used horse placenta treatment on Ghana's Asamoah Gyan after he had been injured and was expected to miss football for four weeks.\n- Asamoah Gyan is a Ghanaian professional footballer who plays as a striker for Kayserispor and serves as captain of the Ghanaian national team.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
